@using LimboDancer.Domains.Asl.Play
@* Pass 28 (ruling R28.1): the SSRs (ruling R17.10), numbered by their place: each one's text, status, the tokens the game reads, the rules it cites,
   and a note. *@
<fieldset class="card-fields" id="edit-ssr">
    <legend>Special rules (SSR)</legend>
    @if (Draft.Rules.Count == 0)
    {
        <p class="muted" id="edit-ssr-none">The card has no special rules.</p>
    }
    <ol class="card-rules-list">
        @for (var index = 0; index < Draft.Rules.Count; index++)
        {
            var at = index;
            var rule = Draft.Rules[at];
            <li @key="rule" id="@($"edit-ssr-{at}")" class="card-rule">
                <div class="card-rule-head">
                    <span class="card-rule-number">SSR @(at + 1)</span>
                    <select id="@($"edit-ssr-{at}-status")" value="@rule.Status" @onchange="@(args => Set(() => rule.Status = Text(args)))" aria-label="@($"SSR {at + 1} status")"
                            class="@($"card-rule-status {rule.Status}")">
                        @foreach (var status in ScenarioCards.RuleStatuses)
                        {
                            <option value="@status">@(status switch { "token" => "read by the game (token)", "game-default" => "played by default", _ => "shown, not enforced" })</option>
                        }
                    </select>
                    <button id="@($"edit-ssr-{at}-up")" type="button" disabled="@(at == 0)" @onclick="@(() => Set(() => Move(at, at - 1)))" aria-label="@($"Move SSR {at + 1} up")">Up</button>
                    <button id="@($"edit-ssr-{at}-remove")" type="button" @onclick="@(() => Set(() => Draft.Rules.Remove(rule)))" aria-label="@($"Remove SSR {at + 1}")">Remove</button>
                </div>
                <textarea id="@($"edit-ssr-{at}-text")" rows="2" @onchange="@(args => Set(() => rule.Text = Text(args)))" value="@rule.Text" aria-label="@($"SSR {at + 1} text")"></textarea>
                <details class="card-fold" open="@(rule.Status == "token")">
                    <summary>Details@(rule.Tokens.Trim().Length > 0 ? $": {rule.Tokens.Trim()}" : string.Empty)</summary>
                    <div class="card-field-row">
                        @* Referee, pass 28: tokens stay as typed whatever the status, so a token left on a rule the game does not read is reported, not dropped. *@
                        <div class="card-field card-field-grow">
                            <label for="@($"edit-ssr-{at}-tokens")" title="read by the game only when the status is token (rulings R16.1, R16.9, R23.5)">Tokens</label>
                            <input id="@($"edit-ssr-{at}-tokens")" value="@rule.Tokens" @onchange="@(args => Set(() => rule.Tokens = Text(args)))" placeholder="@(rule.Status == "token" ? "night:1 weather:rain" : "none")" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-field">
                            <label for="@($"edit-ssr-{at}-rules")" title="registered rule fragments or rulings (ruling R17.2)">Rules cited</label>
                            <input id="@($"edit-ssr-{at}-rules")" value="@rule.Rules" @onchange="@(args => Set(() => rule.Rules = Text(args)))" />
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="card-field-row">
                        <div class="card-field card-field-wide">
                            <label for="@($"edit-ssr-{at}-note")">Note</label>
                            <input id="@($"edit-ssr-{at}-note")" value="@rule.Note" @onchange="@(args => Set(() => rule.Note = Text(args)))" placeholder="@(rule.Status == "not-enforced" ? "why it is not enforced" : string.Empty)" />
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </details>
            </li>
        }
    </ol>
    <button id="edit-ssr-add" type="button" @onclick="@(() => Set(() => Draft.Rules.Add(new RuleDraft())))">Add an SSR</button>
</fieldset>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public CardDraft Draft { get; set; } = default!;

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback Changed { get; set; }

    private static string Text(ChangeEventArgs args) => args.Value as string ?? string.Empty;

    private Task Set(Action change)
    {
        change();
        return Changed.InvokeAsync();
    }

    private void Move(int from, int to)
    {
        var rule = Draft.Rules[from];
        Draft.Rules.RemoveAt(from);
        Draft.Rules.Insert(to, rule);
    }
}
